.TH MARKEE 1 "2026-11-25" "markee 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
markee \- simulated 72x16 24-bit RGB LED matrix display and HTTP/1.1 API server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B markee
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B markee
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B markee
simulates a true-to-size (~6.35-inch wide) 72x16 24-bit RGB LED matrix display
inside a molded desktop enclosure, refreshing at 60 Hz and exposing a local
HTTP/1.1 API (with Keep-Alive, open CORS, SSE events, and a built-in Web
Playground at \fB/ui\fR).
.PP
When invoked with a client subcommand (\fBsay\fR, \fBnotify\fR, \fBgif\fR,
\fBtimer\fR, \fBclock\fR, \fBalert\fR, \fBclear\fR, or \fBinfo\fR),
.B markee
acts as a CLI client talking to an already running instance.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-resolution " " \fIWxH\fR
LED matrix resolution in pixels (default: \fB72x16\fR; range \fB1..1024\fR per
axis).
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-zoom " " \fIfactor\fR
Window zoom multiplier (default: \fB1.0\fR; range \fB0.1..10.0\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-square ", " \-\-circle
Render each LED pixel as a square (default) or circle.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-shape " " \fIstyle\fR
Pixel shape: \fBsquare\fR or \fBcircle\fR.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-monochrome ", " \-\-mono " " \fIcolor\fR
Start with the non-destructive BT.709 perceptual monochrome tint filter enabled
(accepts \fB#rrggbb\fR, \fB0xrrggbb\fR, \fB#rgb\fR, or named colors such as
\fBamber\fR, \fBgreen\fR, \fBred\fR).
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host " " \fIaddr\fR
Bind address for the HTTP server (IPv4, IPv6, or hostname; default:
\fB127.0.0.1\fR).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIport\fR
TCP port to listen on (\fB0..65535\fR; \fB0\fR picks an ephemeral port; default:
\fB8080\fR or \fBMARKEE_PORT\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-token " " \fIsecret\fR
Require \fBAuthorization: Bearer \fIsecret\fR (or \fB?token=\fIsecret\fR) on API
requests. Overrides \fBMARKEE_TOKEN\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-dpi " " \fIvalue\fR
Override monitor logical DPI for physical 6.35-inch sizing.
.TP
.BR \-\-always\-on\-top ", " \-\-topmost
Keep the GUI window floating above other windows. Use
\fB\-\-no\-always\-on\-top\fR to override a config file setting.
.TP
.BR \-\-borderless ", " \-\-frameless
Hide the OS titlebar, use a transparent backdrop, and drag the enclosure to
reposition. Use \fB\-\-no\-borderless\fR to override a config file setting.
.TP
.BR \-\-position ", " \-\-pos " " \fIpos\fR
Set initial window placement using:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
9-point compass directions (case-insensitive): \fBnw\fR, \fBn\fR, \fBne\fR,
\fBw\fR, \fBc\fR, \fBe\fR, \fBsw\fR, \fBs\fR, \fBse\fR (or full words
\fBnorthwest\fR, \fBnorth\fR, etc.).
.IP \(bu 2
Descriptive anchor names: \fBtop-left\fR (\fBtl\fR), \fBtop\fR
(\fBtop-center\fR), \fBtop-right\fR (\fBtr\fR), \fBleft\fR
(\fBmiddle-left\fR/\fBcenter-left\fR), \fBcenter\fR (\fBmiddle\fR),
\fBright\fR (\fBmiddle-right\fR/\fBcenter-right\fR), \fBbottom-left\fR
(\fBbl\fR), \fBbottom\fR (\fBbottom-center\fR), \fBbottom-right\fR (\fBbr\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
Explicit coordinates \fIX,Y\fR in screen pixels, where negative values measure
inward from the right or bottom edge (e.g. \fB\-10,10\fR places the right edge
10 px from the right side and top edge 10 px down; \fB\-0,\-0\fR sits flush
bottom-right), and either axis may be \fBcenter\fR (e.g. \fBcenter,\-20\fR).
.RE
.TP
.BR \-\-corner " " \fIplace\fR
Alias for named \fB\-\-position\fR anchors.
.TP
.BR \-\-case " " \fItheme\fR
Enclosure color theme: \fBwhite\fR (default), \fBcharcoal\fR
(\fBblack\fR/\fBdark\fR), \fBorange\fR, or \fBretro\fR (\fBbeige\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-idle\-dim " " \fIseconds\fR
Automatically fade GUI brightness down after \fIseconds\fR without API writes
or user input.
.TP
.BR \-\-idle\-brightness " " \fI0..100\fR
Target GUI brightness level used by \fB\-\-idle\-dim\fR (default: \fB20\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-demo ", " \-\-blank
Start with the built-in 60 Hz demo animation (\fB\-\-demo\fR) or blank display
(\fB\-\-blank\fR, default).
.TP
.BR \-\-mute ", " \-\-no\-audio
Disable alert sound playback.
.TP
.BR \-\-headless
Run only the HTTP API server and 60 Hz display/audio loop without opening a GUI
window.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIpath\fR
Load default options from an INI configuration file instead of the default path.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-config
Ignore the default configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-\-save\-position
Persist the final GUI window \fBposition = X,Y\fR back to the active config
file on exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.SH CLIENT SUBCOMMANDS
Client subcommands send one request to an already running \fBmarkee\fR and
exit non-zero on failure; they never start a display. The server address and
token come from, in order of precedence: \fB\-H\fR/\fB\-\-host\fR,
\fB\-p\fR/\fB\-\-port\fR, and \fB\-\-token\fR; then \fBMARKEE_HOST\fR,
\fBMARKEE_PORT\fR, and \fBMARKEE_TOKEN\fR; then \fBhost\fR, \fBport\fR, and
\fBtoken\fR in the configuration file (\fB\-\-config\fR \fIpath\fR selects
another file, \fB\-\-no\-config\fR skips it). A wildcard host
(\fB0.0.0.0\fR or \fB::\fR) connects to loopback.
.TP
.BI "draw " "[file|-|json]"
Send a raw \fBPOST /draw\fR JSON operation list (see \fBAPI.md\fR) read from
\fIfile\fR, from standard input (\fB\-\fR, or no argument when input is piped),
or given inline as an argument starting with \fB[\fR or \fB{\fR. Accepts
\fB\-\-transition\fR (\fBfade\fR, \fBdip\fR, \fBslide-left\fR, \fBslide-right\fR, \fBslide-up\fR, \fBslide-down\fR, \fBwipe\fR, \fBwipe-left\fR, \fBwipe-up\fR, \fBwipe-down\fR, \fBsplit\fR, \fBcenter-out\fR, \fBblinds\fR, \fBdissolve\fR) and
\fB\-\-transition\-ms\fR \fI50..5000\fR (default 250).
.TP
.BI "say " "<text>"
Display text on the matrix. Supports \fB\-c\fR/\fB\-\-color\fR, \fB\-\-bg\fR,
\fB\-\-font\fR (\fB4x6\fR, \fB5x7\fR, \fB6x8\fR, \fB8x8\fR, \fBprop\fR),
\fB\-\-scroll\fR, \fB\-\-speed\fR (scroll speed in px/s), \fB\-\-transition\fR
(\fBfade\fR, \fBdip\fR, \fBslide-left\fR, \fBslide-right\fR, \fBslide-up\fR, \fBslide-down\fR, \fBwipe\fR, \fBwipe-left\fR, \fBwipe-up\fR, \fBwipe-down\fR, \fBsplit\fR, \fBcenter-out\fR, \fBblinds\fR, \fBdissolve\fR),
\fB\-\-transition\-ms\fR \fI50..5000\fR (default 250),
\fB\-\-sound\fR/\fB\-\-ding\fR/\fB\-\-chime\fR/\fB\-\-bell\fR,
and \fB\-\-volume 0..100\fR for the sound.
.TP
.BI "notify " "<text>"
Show a transient notification banner and restore the previous display after
\fB\-\-ttl\fR seconds (default: \fB5\fR). Supports \fB\-c\fR/\fB\-\-color\fR,
\fB\-\-bg\fR, \fB\-\-border\fR, \fB\-\-font\fR, \fB\-\-sound\fR, \fB\-\-ding\fR,
\fB\-\-chime\fR, \fB\-\-bell\fR.
.TP
.BI "gif " "<file.gif>"
Upload and play an animated GIF via \fBPOST /animate\fR. Supports
\fB\-\-fill\fR, \fB\-\-fit\fR (\fBcrop\fR, \fBcontain\fR, \fBstretch\fR),
\fB\-\-speed\fR, and \fB\-\-loop\fR.
.TP
.BI "timer " "<duration>"
Start a live 60 Hz countdown widget (e.g. \fB25m\fR, \fB90s\fR, \fB1h30m\fR).
Supports \fB\-c\fR/\fB\-\-color\fR, \fB\-\-bg\fR, \fB\-\-font\fR,
\fB\-\-no\-bar\fR, and \fB\-\-sound\fR/\fB\-\-ding\fR/\fB\-\-chime\fR/\fB\-\-bell\fR.
.TP
.B clock
Display the autonomous digital clock widget. Supports \fB\-c\fR/\fB\-\-color\fR,
\fB\-\-bg\fR, \fB\-\-font\fR, and \fB\-\-format\fR
(\fB24h\fR, \fB24hm\fR, \fB12h\fR, \fB12hm\fR).
.TP
.BI "alert " "[ding|chime|bell]"
Play a synthesized alert sound. Supports \fB\-\-volume 0..100\fR.
.TP
.B clear
Clear the display to black.
.TP
.B info
Print JSON status and capabilities from \fBGET /info\fR.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
In GUI mode:
.TP
.B 1 / 2 / 3
Preview alert sounds (\fBding\fR, \fBchime\fR, \fBbell\fR).
.TP
.B C
Clear display to black.
.TP
.B D
Toggle built-in demo animation.
.TP
.B K
Cycle enclosure case color theme (\fBwhite\fR, \fBcharcoal\fR, \fBorange\fR,
\fBretro\fR).
.TP
.B M
Toggle monochrome phosphor filter (defaults to amber \fB#ffbf00\fR).
.TP
.B P
Toggle LED pixel shape (\fBsquare\fR / \fBcircle\fR).
.TP
.B R
Start or stop animated GIF recording (saves \fBrecording.gif\fR).
.TP
.B S
Save current frame to \fBsnapshot.png\fR.
.TP
.B T
Toggle always-on-top mode.
.TP
.B SPACE / ENTER
Emit an \fBaction\fR button event on \fBGET /events\fR.
.TP
.B + / \-
Adjust simulated GUI brightness in 10% increments.
.TP
.B Q / ESC
Quit.
.SH HTTP API
Main endpoints served on \fBhttp://127.0.0.1:8080\fR by default (see
\fBAPI.md\fR for the full specification):
.TP
.B GET /ui
Built-in single-page Web Playground studio.
.TP
.B GET /info
Resolution, settings, audio state, and frame counter.
.TP
.B POST /draw
Atomic JSON batch of \fBclear\fR, \fBpixel\fR, \fBline\fR, \fBrect\fR,
\fBoval\fR, \fBpolygon\fR, \fBtext\fR, \fBicon\fR, \fBgradient\fR,
\fBprogress\fR, \fBsparkline\fR, \fBclock\fR, \fBcountdown\fR, and \fBimage\fR ops
(optional \fB?transition=\fR and \fB?ttl=\fR).
.TP
.B GET / POST / DELETE /notify
Show, inspect, or dismiss transient notifications with automatic screen restore.
.TP
.B GET / POST / DELETE /frame
Read or write \fIWxH\fR PNGs or raw 24-bit RGB (\fB/frame.rgb\fR).
.TP
.B GET / POST / DELETE /animate
Play animated GIFs (\fB?fill=\fR, \fB?fit=\fR, \fB?speed=\fR, \fB?loop=\fR),
plus \fBPOST /animate/pause\fR, \fB/animate/resume\fR, \fB/animate/speed\fR.
.TP
.B GET / POST /alert
List or trigger \fBding\fR/\fBchime\fR/\fBbell\fR or custom note melodies
(\fB{"melody":"C5:120,E5:120,G5:240"}\fR).
.TP
.B GET / POST /events
JSON long-polling (\fB?since=&wait=\fR) and SSE (\fB?stream=1\fR) event stream.
.TP
.B GET / POST / DELETE /record
Record live matrix frames into an animated GIF89a.
.TP
.B GET / POST / DELETE /idle, /monochrome, /brightness, /fill, /pixel, /demo, /clear
Panel controls and state inspection.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Unless \fB\-\-no\-config\fR is given,
.B markee
automatically reads \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/markee/config.ini\fR (or
\fB~/.config/markee/config.ini\fR) before applying environment variables and CLI
flags. Supported keys: \fBresolution\fR, \fBzoom\fR, \fBshape\fR,
\fBmonochrome\fR, \fBhost\fR, \fBport\fR, \fBtoken\fR, \fBdpi\fR,
\fBalways_on_top\fR, \fBborderless\fR, \fBposition\fR, \fBcorner\fR,
\fBcase\fR, \fBidle_dim\fR, \fBidle_brightness\fR, \fBdemo\fR, \fBmute\fR,
\fBheadless\fR, and \fBsave_position\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MARKEE_HOST
Default host for client subcommands (default: \fB127.0.0.1\fR).
.TP
.B MARKEE_PORT
Default TCP port for server and client subcommands (default: \fB8080\fR).
.TP
.B MARKEE_TOKEN
Optional Bearer authentication token shared by server and client subcommands.
Overrides \fBtoken\fR in the config file; \fB\-\-token\fR overrides it.
Open the Web Playground as \fB/ui?token=\fIsecret\fR when a token is set.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for \fBmarkee/config.ini\fR (defaults to \fB~/.config\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/markee/config.ini
Default user configuration file.
.TP
.I snapshot.png
Output file written when pressing \fBS\fR in GUI mode.
.TP
.I recording.gif
Output file written when toggling recording with \fBR\fR in GUI mode.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Floating borderless charcoal widget in the top-right corner
markee --borderless --always-on-top --case charcoal --position NE

# Horizontally centered near the top edge with amber phosphor tint
markee --position center,60 --monochrome amber

# Drive a running instance via client subcommands
markee say "BUILD OK" --color green --chime
markee timer 25m --color amber --sound bell
markee gif examples/cat_chase-72x16.gif --fill white
cat examples/ops.json | markee draw
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
Full HTTP API documentation is installed alongside this package in
\fBAPI.md\fR and \fBREADME.md\fR.
